// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
// Donor: Roslyn's `EatToken` / `EatTokenAsKind` pair for the QUESTION -- a
// parser reading broken input needs two different answers to "the token is not
// here". NOT taken: Roslyn's skipped-token trivia and its error-recovery
// ranking; this subset plants one lossless Err leaf and lets `check` decide
// whether the gap is worth saying.
// Role: layer 2 (parse) -- taking a token that is EXPECTED at this position,
// and the difference between "optional here" and "required here". That
// difference is registry #809 and #815: for a year every closing bracket AND
// eighteen other required positions were taken by the optional door, so
// `fn main() {` with no `}` and `type { n int }` with no name both compiled
// with exit code 0 and not one diagnostic.
// Used by: parse.nv, expr.nv, decls.nv -- every place a comma, a keyword, a
// name or a bracket is taken.
// Guarded by: check-novac-required-token-door.py (a required token kind
// through the optional door is red, base zero; so is ZERO calls of the
// mandatory door, which is how a rename would blind it), plus the class tests
// "an unclosed bracket is refused, not accepted in silence (#809)" and "a
// token the grammar requires is refused when absent (#815)".
// novac/src/parse/expect.nv -- is this token optional here, or required.

module novac.parse

import ../lex.{TokenKind}
import ../tree.{Node, NodeKind}

/// Take the token if it is the one wanted, and say ONCE what it means when it
/// is not.
///
/// The phrase `if @peek() == X { kids.push(@take()) }` stood at fifty-four
/// places in this parser: every optional comma and keyword. Each was an
/// incomplete branching (P31) whose missing half means the same thing
/// everywhere -- the token is optional here, there is nothing to take, and
/// that is a valid outcome. Fifty-four empty `else` comments would say it
/// fifty-four times; a named door says it once, and the call site gets
/// shorter into the bargain.
///
/// A CLOSING bracket is not one of those, and saying it was is #809: this
/// door used to take `}` too, so a file ending mid-body was accepted in
/// silence. Closers go through `@push_closer` below, and the guard
/// check-novac-closer-mandatory keeps them there.
fn Cursor mut @push_if(mut kids []Node, k TokenKind) -> () {
    if @peek() == k {
        kids.push(@take())
    } else {
        // Nothing to take: the token is optional at this position. This is
        // THE empty branch P31 asks to be named, and it is named here for
        // every call site at once.
    }
}

/// Take a token the grammar REQUIRES here; plant a gap when it is not there.
///
/// The twin of `@push_if`, and the difference is the whole of registry #809 and
/// #815. `@push_if` means "optional at this position, and absence is a valid
/// outcome" -- true of a trailing comma. This one means "nothing else can stand
/// here and still be this form", which covers every closing bracket (its opener
/// has already been consumed) and eighteen other positions: a name, an `=`, a
/// `=>`, the `{` of a match, the `(` of a signature, the `in` of a for-loop.
///
/// Taken with the optional door, `fn main() {` with no `}` compiled with exit
/// code 0 and not one diagnostic, and `type { n int }` compiled with no name at
/// all.
///
/// ONE door, not two, and the code is what says so: while the parser tried to
/// tell a cause from its wake, a closer needed different treatment from a name.
/// It could not -- the parser meets a missing token BEFORE its recovery marks
/// the run that caused it, so on `fn main junk here () { }` the refusal about
/// the absent `(` came out first and the one about the junk second. The
/// decision moved to `check.tell_gap_if_silent`, where order does not exist,
/// and the two doors' bodies became identical. They are one door now.
fn Cursor mut @push_expected(mut kids []Node, k TokenKind) -> () {
    if @peek() == k {
        kids.push(@take())
    } else {
        // Nothing else can stand here and still be this form. The zero-width
        // Err keeps the tree lossless and hands `check` a position; WHETHER
        // it is worth saying is the checker's call, and it makes it once for
        // both doors (`tell_gap_if_silent`).
        //
        // THE LEAF CARRIES THE KIND THAT WAS WANTED (registry #850, donor
        // Roslyn `EatTokenAsKind`, named in this file's header from the start).
        // Until now `k` died here, so the checker could only say "this is not a
        // form of the language" -- true, and useless to someone who left out a
        // `)`. The leaf is safe to give a real kind because it lives INSIDE an
        // Err branch, and every consumer of the tree filters DIRECT children by
        // kind; nothing but the refusal reader ever looks in there.
        kids.push(@node(NodeKind.Err, []Node.of(@missing_of(k))))
    }
}
